WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:03.230
Speaker 1: Let's talk about political fundraising.

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:06.710
We've been looking at polling, but we have
not been looking at fundraising.

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:08.370
The second quarter just ended.

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:11.490
The second quarter is April, May and June.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.110
And we have some very interesting new fundraising
data.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:18.500
I do not yet have Joe Biden's fundraising
data for the second quarter.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.930
When I have it, I will tell you what it is.

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:26.939
But Donald Trump's fundraising has exploded
significantly in Q2, assuming, of course,

00:00:26.939 --> 00:00:30.250
that the Trump campaign is being honest in
their reporting.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:36.100
Trump pulled in per politico more than $35
million in the second quarter.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:40.670
That is nearly double what Trump raised in
Q1 and suggests.

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:45.940
Politico writes that the indictments are helping
with fundraising, and the article goes into

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.199
detail in Q1.

00:00:48.199 --> 00:00:52.410
Trump raised just under $19 million in Q2.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:55.090
Trump raised more than $35 million.

00:00:55.090 --> 00:01:01.269
Important to note, the joint fundraising committee
is split between Trump's official campaign

00:01:01.269 --> 00:01:04.239
and his leadership PAC, Save America.

00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:09.049
At least in theory, the Save America PAC is
meant to raise money for people that Trump

00:01:09.049 --> 00:01:12.409
endorses or supports.

00:01:12.409 --> 00:01:18.150
The official did not break down how much of
that 35 million went to Trump versus the PAC.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:25.450
But the most recent fundraising solicitations
direct 90% of each donation to Trump's campaign

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:28.670
and 10% to the Save America PAC.

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:35.240
The PAC, by the way, also lately is focusing
spending on non-campaign activity, like paying

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:38.090
for Trump's legal bills.

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:41.340
So there are a few different things to talk
about here.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:47.509
First and foremost, the average donation was
$34 in $0.20.

00:01:47.509 --> 00:01:49.719
We have people.

00:01:49.719 --> 00:01:57.869
Who can only afford to give about 30 bucks
paying for a billionaire's legal fees.

00:01:57.869 --> 00:02:03.490
A billionaire who has a private jet, they
are sending money to a guy with a private

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:06.289
plane for his legal fees.

00:02:06.289 --> 00:02:10.619
Because of all of the crimes he allegedly
committed and all they can really do, it's

00:02:10.619 --> 00:02:17.680
30 bucks because statistically, they can't
meet an unexpected $400 expense that they

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:20.280
might be presented with.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.800
That's insane.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:22.940
That is insane.

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:24.150
And grift after grift.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:26.110
You know, I hate to do this.

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:28.660
Sort of, like, caveat emptor.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:32.180
A fool and their money are soon parted.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:34.709
We can't have a nanny state protecting these
people.

00:02:34.709 --> 00:02:37.610
Like, I don't want to go in that direction.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:42.349
But after the grift of 2016, where Trump raised
money, money, money, despite saying, I don't

00:02:42.349 --> 00:02:46.350
really need any money, I'm rich enough to
run on my own with all of these promises that

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:47.880
he didn't meet.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:51.971
And then he ran again in 2020 saying, I'm
making the same promises all over again, even

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.750
though I didn't meet them in the first campaign.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:54.750
This time I will.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:56.629
And people donate and then Trump loses.

00:02:56.629 --> 00:03:00.800
And then there's this Hey, now I need your
money in order to overturn elections and do

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:04.599
forensic audits where we're going to look
ballot by ballot for bamboo fibers or barbecue

00:03:04.599 --> 00:03:09.650
sauce or whatever the case they were looking
for and also for filing lawsuits.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:14.239
And then half of that 70% of that went to
paying Trump's campaign bills.

00:03:14.239 --> 00:03:15.750
GRift after grift after grift.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:16.750
And now he's doing it again.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:20.159
And they're still donating money for legal
fees.

00:03:20.159 --> 00:03:24.659
At this point, I don't think there's anyone
who can protect these people, and probably

00:03:24.659 --> 00:03:26.300
we shouldn't even continue trying.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.379
I want to hear from you on that question.

00:03:28.379 --> 00:03:33.019
Should these folks who continue to donate
money to the obvious grift, should we even

00:03:33.019 --> 00:03:35.459
care at this point or at some point?

00:03:35.459 --> 00:03:39.599
Is it a matter of personal responsibility
like Republicans love to say and they need

00:03:39.599 --> 00:03:42.569
to be parted with their money if they are
going to fall for it again?

00:03:42.569 --> 00:03:44.000
Let me know what you think.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:47.010
We are going to keep an eye on the Biden fundraising
numbers.

