in the Senate.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:17.900
The third of the Senate that happens to be
up for reelection in 2024 is not particularly

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.500
good for Democrats.

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:27.190
What is very interesting is that a number
of a number of prominent Democrats are doing

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:29.270
really well in terms of fundraising.

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:32.870
Senator Bob Casey in Pennsylvania has raised
more than $4 million.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:35.509
That's his best fundraising quarter ever.

00:04:35.509 --> 00:04:39.970
Senator Tammy Baldwin from Wisconsin, first
openly LGBT woman in the Senate, raised over

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:41.150
$3 million.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:42.960
That is also a record high.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:46.680
Adam Schiff broke the record for second quarter
Senate fundraising.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:50.410
Remember, he's a member of Congress, but he's
running for Dianne Feinstein seat, which he

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:51.479
will be vacating.

00:04:51.479 --> 00:04:55.560
These are stunning, stunning, stunning numbers.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:58.750
But there are many Republicans who are doing
well as well.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:06.340
In Nevada, retired U.S. Army Captain Sam Brown
is likely to launch a Senate campaign against

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:07.990
